hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"196","Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Mukhurami and Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, they said: Yahya bin Adam told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zur bin Hubaysh. He said: I went to Safwan bin Assal Al-Muradi and asked him about wiping over the socks. He said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And peace be upon him, so he commanded us not to remove our slippers for three days, that is, while traveling, except for ritual impurity, but also for defecation, urination, and sleep.”"
